# Unslop UI Standard

Goal: every visual choice is decided for this product, not a default. "Nothing wrong, nothing decided" is a failure.

Symptom list with sources: `docs/design/unslop-features.md`.

Fix root causes in the existing design tokens/styles; never stack overrides, !important, or one-off classes on top.
Keep existing structure and data unless asked; change the look, not the behavior.

## 0. Pre-flight: decide direction first (before writing code)
- State in 1-2 lines: product, audience, primary job of this screen.
- Write a compact token plan: 4-6 named hex colors, 1-2 typefaces with roles, spacing scale, radius scale, layout concept (alignment).
- Check the plan against the defaults list in §1. If any part looks like what you'd produce for any similar app, revise it and say why.
- Pick ONE place to be bold. Everything else stays quiet.
- Reuse existing tokens (CSS variables / theme file). Add or change tokens there, not inline.

## 1. Banned defaults (don't, unless the brief explicitly asks)
- Purple / neon / purple-to-blue gradients, glowing blobs, floating gradients, neon glow.
- Heavy glassmorphism / backdrop blur as decoration.
- Cream bg (~#F4F1EA) + serif display + terracotta (~#D97757) accent.
- Near-black (#0B0B0B/#111) + single acid-green/vermilion accent as a reflex.
- Same soft shadow (rgba(0,0,0,.1)) under every card; drop shadows for decoration.
- Cards nested in cards. Content chopped into identical rounded cards.
- Pill-shaped cards; one border-radius on everything.
- Rounded-square icon tile above every heading; emoji as icons; colored circle/square behind icons.
- Gray text on colored backgrounds.
- Inter (or any reflex font) for everything.
- One word in a headline set in italic/bold/another color.
- Tracked-out ALL-CAPS eyebrow labels; unnecessary labels above content.
- "A · B · C" meta strings, "WORD — fragment" labels, "→" appended to every link/button, monospace for small labels by reflex.
- 01/02/03 numbering when content is not a real sequence.
- Hero = big number + small label + stats + gradient accent.
- Four KPIs in four identical boxes.
- Fade-and-slide-up on every section; hover animation on every card.
- Emoji, "!!", hype copy, colorful badges.

## 2. Color
- Use the planned 4-6 color palette only; tokens, not literal hex in components.
- Default to calm neutrals (light or dark); spend color on data and state, not decoration.
- Text contrast >= WCAG AA (4.5:1 body, 3:1 large).

## 3. Typography
- 1-2 families, deliberately chosen; if two, clearly distinct.
- Fixed type scale with intentional weights; clear heading hierarchy, no skipped levels.
- Line length < 80 characters; serif body gets slightly more line-height.
- Sentence case for labels and buttons.

## 4. Spacing & layout
- 4px base unit; use steps 8 / 16 / 24 (and multiples). No arbitrary values (13px, 22px).
- Vary spacing to show grouping (tight inside a group, larger between groups); not uniform everywhere.
- Don't over-pad cards or leave gaps too wide; don't cramp either.
- Equal side margins; no section shoved to one side; no random blank stretches.
- Avoid the uniform same-size grid by reflex; size areas by importance.
- Separate viewing UI from editing UI. Non-buttons must not look clickable.
- First screen has a clear title. Remove anything the screen doesn't need.

## 5. Shape, borders, depth
- Radius scale by hierarchy (e.g. 4 / 8 / 12px; 8px default for controls/panels). No pills except true chips/tags.
- Prefer 1px borders in a neutral token over shadows for separation.
- Flat surfaces; at most one elevation level for overlays (menus, modals).

## 6. Icons & imagery
- One monochrome icon set, consistent stroke and size, no background tiles.
- Fewer icons; only where they speed recognition.
- Real images/photos (credited) over letter-only avatars or generic illustrations.

## 7. Data display
- Tabular numbers (`font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums`), right-aligned numeric columns, aligned figures.
- Give each metric the visual that explains it (gauge for a rate, ring for budget used, line/area for trends).
- Calm, precise status labels instead of colorful badges.
- Never drop columns on mobile to fit; scroll or restack.

## 8. Motion
- Motion answers user actions (open, expand, confirm) and shows what changed.
- At most one orchestrated non-user-triggered moment per page.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.

## 9. Copy
- Plain user words, active voice, no filler, no selling. Name things by what users understand.
- CTA says what happens ("Save changes", not "Submit"); same action keeps the same name across the flow.
- Errors say what happened and how to fix it; no apologies, no vagueness. Empty states invite the next action.
- Cut explanations the UI already makes obvious.

## 10. Japanese UI
- Specify Japanese font stack and typesetting explicitly; check missing glyphs.
- Natural line breaks (no orphaned characters); tune letter-spacing.
- Fix mixed Japanese/Latin spacing and numerals; no leftover English labels; Japanese units and order.

## 11. Accessibility & responsive
- Visible keyboard focus on every interactive element.
- Responsive down to 375px; nav folds away on phone.
- Avoid CSS specificity fights (section vs element selectors cancelling padding/margin).
- Handle overflow, long text, i18n, error and empty states.

## 12. Final self-review checklist (run before saying done)
- [ ] Direction + token plan written, and checked against §1.
- [ ] No item from §1 present (grep for gradients, blur, box-shadow, emoji, uppercase, Inter).
- [ ] All colors/spacing/radius come from tokens; no new overrides or !important added.
- [ ] Spacing values are on the 4px grid (8/16/24...).
- [ ] No card inside a card; borders 1px; radius follows the scale.
- [ ] Numbers use tabular-nums and align.
- [ ] Copy: no emoji/hype; CTAs name the result; errors are actionable.
- [ ] Contrast AA, focus visible, reduced motion respected.
- [ ] Screenshots taken at desktop, tablet, mobile widths; top 3 problems fixed (up to 3 rounds).
- [ ] Removed one more unnecessary element before finishing.
